    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "Relates an intended learner profile to the HETO practitioner role class whose bearers the profile describes."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HETO 0.3.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

helo:0000007 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "concept understanding goal"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A learning goal that states which concepts, health economics concepts or learning topics, a learner is intended to understand, and that is met by remembering and understanding them, including how methods work (interpreting, exemplifying, classifying, summarising, inferring, comparing and explaining), not by carrying out a procedure. It is the only kind of learning goal a learning pathway has."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Remember and Understand in the revised Bloom taxonomy (Krathwohl 2002). Explaining can be harder than executing, so understanding goals are a different kind of goal, not a lower tier. A goal at the Analyse or Evaluate level is typed by how it is met, by understanding concepts or by carrying out a procedure on a case."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief; Krathwohl 2002" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf helo:0000006 ;
    owl:disjointWith helo:0000008 .

helo:4000004 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000005 ;
    rdfs:label "outcomes researcher"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An intended learner profile of a person who measures or values the health outcomes of care, such as survival and quality of life, for research or for appraisal."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "The Semantic Layer for Health Economics, course outline draft for Michelle Ashley and Darrin Baines, 18 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    owl:differentFrom helo:4000005,
        helo:4000006 .

helo:4000023 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000014 ;
    rdfs:label "proposed from an unreviewed HEO relationship"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A prerequisite status of a prerequisite relationship derived only from HEO relationships that HEO 2.0.0 still records as unreviewed, held apart from the other proposals until HEO reviews them."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HELO 0.2.0 review B (learning design and content), 19 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> .

helo:4000032 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite from HEO depends on"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A prerequisite derivation rule by which a HEO depends on relationship from one concept to another gives the proposal that the second concept is understood before the first."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "HEO marks depends on for learning. It holds one relationship in HEO 2.0.0."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HEO 2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    owl:differentFrom helo:4000033,
        helo:4000034 ;
    helo:9000014 heo:dependsOn .

helo:0000011 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "curriculum"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity that groups ordered course modules into one course of study, with its intended learners and its learning outcomes, such as a course on the semantic layer for health economics."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Unlike a learning pathway, a curriculum may have task capability goals, because a course can train learners to carry out tasks. A curriculum usually holds goals of both kinds."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Christou et al. 2025; The Semantic Layer for Health Economics, course outline draft for Michelle Ashley and Darrin Baines, 18 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000033 .

helo:0000013 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "publication status"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An information content entity stating whether a learning pathway, a curriculum or a course module is published or is still a draft."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Ashley M. How the knowledge map works, notes for the site developer, 12 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000030 .

helo:4000033 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite from HEO assumes"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A prerequisite derivation rule by which a HEO assumes relationship from a method or model to an assumption gives the proposal that the assumption is understood no later than the method or model, so that the two may be taught in one step."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "HEO marks assumes for learning. Assumptions are usually taught with their method, so a pair in one step agrees with the pathway and only an assumption taught later conflicts (curator decision, 19 October 2026, after review B S2)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HEO 2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    owl:differentFrom helo:4000034 ;
    helo:9000014 heo:assumes .

helo:0000006 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "learning goal"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An objective specification that states what a learner is intended to reach by following a learning pathway, a curriculum or a course module."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000005 .

helo:4000005 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000005 ;
    rdfs:label "economic modeller"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An intended learner profile of a person who designs, builds, runs or checks economic models."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "modeller"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief; HETO 0.3.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    owl:differentFrom helo:4000006 ;
    helo:9000008 heto:0000041 .

helo:4000006 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000005 ;
    rdfs:label "policy maker"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An intended learner profile of a person who takes or advises on decisions about health policy, funding or access, and who uses health economic evidence rather than producing it."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "No pathway or curriculum is stated to be for policy makers yet. Open question for Darrin Baines."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> .

helo:4000034 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        helo:0000010 ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite from HEO used to calculate"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A prerequisite derivation rule by which a HEO used to calculate relationship from an input to a result gives the weaker proposal that the input is understood before the result, only where the input is part of what the result means, read as the HEO definition of the result naming the input."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "HEO marks used to calculate for formal inference and navigation, not for learning, so HELO keeps these proposals as a separate weaker tier (curator decision, 19 October 2026). An input that is only one way of computing the result, such as cumulative hazard for a transition probability, gives no proposal (review B S1)."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HEO 2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    helo:9000014 heo:usedToCalculate .

helo:9000014 a owl:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:label "is derived from HEO property"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "Relates a prerequisite derivation rule to the HEO relationship type it reads."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HEO 2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

helo:0000014 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite status"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An information content entity stating how far a prerequisite relationship has been reviewed, as proposed from HEO, proposed from an unreviewed HEO relationship, accepted by a curator or rejected by a curator."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000030 .

helo:0000010 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite derivation rule"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity stating from which kind of HEO relationship a prerequisite relationship is derived, and which of the two related concepts is to be understood first."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000033 .

helo:0000012 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "course module"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity that is one ordered unit of exactly one curriculum, with the learning topics, HEO concepts and material it uses."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A directive information entity like the curriculum it is part of."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "module"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Christou et al. 2025; The Semantic Layer for Health Economics, course outline draft for Michelle Ashley and Darrin Baines, 18 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty helo:1000024 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom helo:0000011 ],
        obo:IAO_0000033 .

helo:0000005 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "intended learner profile"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An information content entity that describes a kind of learner for whom a learning pathway or a curriculum is intended, by role or background, such as a student or a health technology assessment analyst. It describes an audience, not a person or a role that a person bears."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Profiles may overlap, an economic modeller is usually also a health economist, and student is a stage rather than a role, so a pathway may be for several profiles. A profile may name the HETO role whose bearers it describes, through has corresponding HETO role. The profile is information about an audience and the HETO role is a role in reality, so the two are related by an annotation and neither is a kind of the other."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "intended learner"@en,
        "persona"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; Christou et al. 2025" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000030 .

helo:0000009 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "prerequisite relationship"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A data entity recording that understanding one HEO concept is needed, or proposed to be needed, before another HEO concept can be understood, with the HEO relationships it was derived from, its status and whether the learning pathways order the two concepts the same way."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A record, so a data entity, as the family puts its records. In HELO 0.2.0 every prerequisite relationship is a proposal derived from HEO relationships and none is asserted as fact. Proposals are not transitive for learning beyond one step, so a long chain is not a required route. A learning pathway itself asserts only the order of its steps and the concepts it builds on. Each record names the pathways whose order agrees with it, the pathways whose order conflicts with it and the pathways that put both concepts in one step."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "prerequisite record"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "HELO 0.2.0 design (best practice), Michelle Ashley with Claude, 19 October 2026; HEO 2.0.0" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf obo:IAO_0000027 .

helo:0000002 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "learning step"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity that is one ordered part of exactly one learning pathway, naming the topic studied at that point and the HEO concepts it covers, as core concepts to learn and optional concepts that go further."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "A step directs what to study at one point of its pathway, so it is a directive information entity like the pathway it is part of. A step is identified by its pathway and its topic, not by its position, so a step keeps its identifier when the steps of a pathway are reordered. Its position is the datatype value has step position."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Ashley M. How the knowledge map works, notes for the site developer, 12 October 2026; HealthEconomics.wiki Learning Layer, /api/pathways and the pathway framework pages, read 19 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom helo:0000007 ;
            owl:onProperty helo:1000012 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty helo:1000002 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom helo:0000001 ],
        obo:IAO_0000033 .

helo:0000001 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "learning pathway"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000114 obo:IAO_0000125 ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity that sets out an ordered series of learning steps through which a learner builds understanding of related health economics concepts, from foundational concepts to more advanced ones. A learning pathway prepares a learner for health economics tasks but does not train the learner to carry them out."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000116 "Darrin Baines's scope of 18 October 2026. Pathways help people understand concepts in a logical order from core to advanced, and they do not teach how to carry out tasks. The line follows the revised Bloom taxonomy (Krathwohl 2002). A pathway may aim at remembering and understanding, including explaining how a method works, which is understanding of procedural knowledge, and it may not train the carrying out of a procedure. A pathway is a plan of study, not a HETO task. HELO keeps the two apart in three ways. A learning pathway has only concept understanding goals (an OWL restriction and a SHACL rule), its relationship to a HETO task is prepares for task and never one of training, and a learning pathway may not also be typed as a HETO task specification (a SHACL rule). The Curriculum KG learning path is close in meaning and is mapped in SSSOM, not used as a parent, because its axioms require every learning step to have exactly one next step and one previous step, which a last step does not have."@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000117 "Michelle Ashley (drafted with Claude)" ;
    obo:IAO_0000118 "pathway"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000119 "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief; Ashley M. How the knowledge map works, notes for the site developer, 12 October 2026" ;
    dcterms:contributor <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:allValuesFrom helo:0000007 ;
            owl:onProperty helo:1000012 ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty helo:1000001 ;
            owl:someValuesFrom helo:0000002 ],
        obo:IAO_0000033 ;
    helo:9000001 "Learning pathways build understanding, not hands-on skills."@en .

<https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9502-4678>,
        <https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0231-3731> ;
    dcterms:description "The Health Economics Learning Ontology (HELO) states the learning pathways of HealthEconomics.wiki as an ontology, ordered learning steps that build understanding of HEO concepts from foundational to advanced, with their pathway frameworks, intended learner profiles, learning goals and the prerequisite relationships proposed from HEO, and gives courses such as the semantic layer course a shared structure of curricula and course modules. Learning pathways build understanding, not hands-on skills. They prepare a learner for the tasks of the Health Economics Task Ontology (HETO) and do not train them. Classes are information entities of IAO under BFO 2020, and the Curriculum KG Ontology and schema.org are mapped in SSSOM, not imported. HELO here is the Health Economics Learning Ontology of HealthEconomics.wiki. It is not the HypothEsis and Law Ontology, also called HELO (Soldatova et al. 2013), and is unrelated to it."@en ;
    dcterms:issued "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:publisher "Intelligent Parameters Ltd" ;
    dcterms:source "Baines D. Scope of the learning pathways ontology, 18 October 2026, passed on by Michelle Ashley in the HELO 0.2.0 brief" ;
    dcterms:title "Health Economics Learning Ontology (HELO)"@en ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "helo" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/HELO_" ;
    rdfs:comment "Version 0.1.0 alpha, fixed in place after three independent reviews of 19 October 2026. Not uploaded. Every term has the curation status pending final vetting, and every proposal requires discussion. HELO here is the Health Economics Learning Ontology of HealthEconomics.wiki. It is not the HypothEsis and Law Ontology, also called HELO (Soldatova et al. 2013), and is unrelated to it."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://healtheconomics.wiki/knowledge-map> ;
    owl:imports <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/bfo/2020/bfo-core.owl>,
        <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/0.2.0/imports/heao-linking-kinds.owl>,
        <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/0.2.0/imports/iao-extract.owl> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo/0.2.0/helo.owl> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.2.0" .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The HELO profile health economist describes people who bear this HETO role. HELO defines health economist as \"An intended learner profile of a person who works in health economics, in research, in practice or in government.\" and HETO defines health economics practitioner role as \"A role borne by a person that is realised when that person carries out health economics work, such as framing, costing, modelling, analysing or reporting an economic evaluation.\". The profile is information about an audience and the role is borne by people, so the profile describes the role's bearers, a representational relationship."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000008 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000002 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heto:0000040 ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The rule reads the HEO relationship type Assumes and records a proposed order of learning, so it represents HEO relationships and does not change them. HEO marks assumes for learning. Assumptions are usually taught with their method, so a pair in one step agrees with the pathway and only an assumption taught later conflicts (curator decision, 19 October 2026, after review B S2)."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000014 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000033 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heo:assumes ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The rule reads the HEO relationship type Used to calculate and records a proposed order of learning, so it represents HEO relationships and does not change them. HEO marks used to calculate for formal inference and navigation, not for learning, so HELO keeps these proposals as a separate weaker tier (curator decision, 19 October 2026). An input that is only one way of computing the result, such as cumulative hazard for a transition probability, gives no proposal (review B S1)."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000014 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000034 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heo:usedToCalculate ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The rule reads the HEO relationship type Prerequisite for and records a proposed order of learning, so it represents HEO relationships and does not change them. HEO defines prerequisite for as a learning dependency and marks it for learning."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000014 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000030 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heo:prerequisiteFor ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The rule reads the HEO relationship type Depends on and records a proposed order of learning, so it represents HEO relationships and does not change them. HEO marks depends on for learning. It holds one relationship in HEO 2.0.0."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000014 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000032 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heo:dependsOn ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ;
    owl:members ( helo:0000001 helo:0000002 helo:0000003 helo:0000004 helo:0000005 helo:0000006 helo:0000009 helo:0000010 helo:0000011 helo:0000012 helo:0000013 helo:0000014 ) .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The HELO profile economic modeller describes people who bear this HETO role. HELO defines economic modeller as \"An intended learner profile of a person who designs, builds, runs or checks economic models.\" and HETO defines economic modeller role as \"A health economics practitioner role that is realised when its bearer designs, builds, runs or checks an economic model.\". The profile is information about an audience and the role is borne by people, so the profile describes the role's bearers, a representational relationship."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000008 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000005 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heto:0000041 ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    rdfs:comment "The rule reads the HEO relationship type Is foundation for and records a proposed order of learning, so it represents HEO relationships and does not change them. HEO defines is foundation for as a basic idea on which another is built and marks it for learning."@en ;
    owl:annotatedProperty helo:9000014 ;
    owl:annotatedSource helo:4000031 ;
    owl:annotatedTarget heo:isFoundationFor ;
    heao:9000001 heao:4000002 .


<https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#priorVersion> <https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontology/helo/0.1.0/helo.owl> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Version 0.2.0 moves every HELO address from https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontology/helo to https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/helo, so the ontology identifier, its version identifier and its terms match the ontology page on the site. Every class, property, definition and axiom is the same as in 0.1.0, and the imports now point to the family releases made at the same time (HEO 2.0.0, RHEO 0.4.0, OHEO 0.3.0, HETO 0.3.0, HEAO 0.2.0, HEMO 0.2.0, HELO 0.2.0, HEIRO 0.2.0). The old /ontology/ addresses are retired and are not redirected."@en .
